    fix(ops): classify a manifest-less shell toolkit as cli in the fleet ops census (CF-206)
    
    ~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py derives docs_only from the absence of a language
    manifest and then returns zero checks for that kind, so code-factory - eight tracked
    provisioning scripts under scripts/, a harness/ adapter tree and a tests/selftest.sh gate,
    plus every node they provision - was classified docs and judged on nothing.
    
    Measured fleet delta at this commit: docs=45 -> 40, cli=2 -> 7, and exactly the five
    shell-toolkit families the row named (code-factory, code-factory-duckbrain,
    fleet-ops-check, h3, my-project) are now judged as cli. flag=43 -> 44.
    
    The live file is unversioned, so the change ships as
    patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.patch (sha256 f7f1dfc3...) with its fixture harness
    patches/fleet-ops-shell-toolkit.test.py: 10 arms covering the docs/cli/service
    regression, tracked-vs-untracked scripts, the two-script threshold, the toolkit basis
    evidence, and census rc=0/rc=1 semantics.
    
    Also fixed here: the deploy-doc check matched only the lowercase docs/operations.md, so
    turning it on reported a false P3 against this very repo, which carries docs/OPERATIONS.md.
    Basename matching is now case-insensitive.
